From 76d801e4221ddf869e5e24b7e614a16c951dbfaa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 17:18:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add CSV-based geolocation engine, unified into the detections
 table

Wires the uploaded geolocation_engine.py in as a second ingestion path
(POST /logs/geolocate_csv) for detections already produced by an external/
offline detector, joined against a nav CSV by ping_id. Results are written
into the same `detections` table as the image/YOLO/VAE pipeline (source_
format="csv_detections"), so they appear in /map, /detections, and reports
identically regardless of source.

Fixes one bug found relative to the uploaded script: depth_m now includes
altitude_m (object depth = vehicle depth + altitude, since the object rests
near the seafloor below the vehicle), matching the intended physical model
instead of just relaying the vehicle's own depth.

Also finishes the footprint-geometry feature from the prior session: wires
geometry_mode (auto/point_only/footprint_only) through GET /logs/{id}/map
as a query param, with a 400 on an invalid value instead of a 500.
